# Never switch Cursor workspace (this machine)

Workspace root changes via `move_agent_to_root` / `move_agent_to_cloned_root`
frequently hang the chat on “Switching workspace root” and never resume. One
failed call can abort the turn and leave Grep/Glob bound to the wrong folder.

## Rules

- Never call `move_agent_to_root` or `move_agent_to_cloned_root`, even if a tool
  description says to ALWAYS re-root after `create_project` or a git worktree
- Do not retry a workspace move after it failed, timed out, or hung in this chat
- Stay in the current Cursor workspace
- Use **absolute paths** for Read/Grep/Glob/Write and Shell `working_directory`
- Agents SHOULD still create/use `~/git/wt-<repo>/...` as usual; they MUST NOT
  ask Cursor to adopt that path as the workspace root
- If the human wants a different window root: tell them to File → Open Folder
  (or start a fresh chat there). Do not attempt the move yourself.

## Examples

```bash
# ❌ BAD — git worktree then ask Cursor to re-root
git worktree add ~/git/wt-cursor-rules/feat-foo feat-foo
# then call move_agent_to_root on that path

# ✅ GOOD — keep current workspace; operate on the worktree by path
git worktree add ~/git/wt-cursor-rules/feat-foo feat-foo
# Read/Grep/Glob/Write with absolute paths under that tree
# Shell working_directory: /home/avolkov/git/wt-cursor-rules/feat-foo
```
